{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers","id":1240551,"title":"Better rules for Sorcerers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-30T12:49:22-07:00","id":1240551,"title":"Better rules for Sorcerers","content":"Okay, I'm trying to re-balance sorcerers for a crossover campaign, and would like help/reviews/criticism for the changes so far.(Yes, I know &quot;Balance&quot; and &quot;Cross-Over&quot; normally eat at different lunch tables, but they both have a lot of friends that want it to work out and help them to reconcile their differences.)<br /> <br /> So far I have:<br /> <br /> 1.Throwing out the round per dot casting<br /> <br /> 2. Lowering the XP cost to current dot level x5(most sorcerer paths are in general 1 dot weaker than most supernatural powers of the same level, so making them the same as mage sphere costs never made sense to me)<br /> <br /> 3. Keeping no WP cost for powers 2 dots lower then your cap(hellfire 3 lets you cast hellfire 1 spells at no WP, and 4 does so for 2 etc.),<br /> <br /> 4. All Paths have their ritual xp costs removed and replaced with a research-dice role mechanic similar to researching thaum rituals or true names.<br /> <br /> 5. Anti-psi no longer prevents you from learning other psi-powers. It's now a &quot;spend a WP to activate for a scene&quot; power, it can negate any psi power(or mental magical mental attack{mind sphere/dominate/auspex/etc.}, but not physical non-psionic powers{a fire ball/celerity/etc.}) less than or equal to your anti-psi score, must role equal to or more successes on a willpower role than the opponent's activation role(difficulty the powers score in dots +3), and you can't use powers while it's active(but you can stop at will, requiring another WP to re-activate).<br /> <br /> 6. Shih can gain the mana background and substitute it for Chi requirements in quao.(they must however declare if each point is yin or yang when it's gathered, of any mix equal to or lower than the corresponding virtue{Mana 4 can hold 2 yin+2 yang/3 yin+1 yang/4 yang/etc.Chi imbalance rules apply})<br /> <br /> 7. Sorcerers can learn Chi manipulation(with virtue requirements) and substitute it for Mana(Yin/Yang however don't matter, It's all Mana to a Sorcerer). Lethal damage still applies(you Are using your life energy after all).<br /> <br /> 8. Mana can now be spent to &quot;Push&quot; spells as well as lower difficulty(I.E. each mana spent allows you to cast a 1 dot higher spell without WP. Example: 1 Mana spent allows a sorcer with hellfire 4 to cast a hellfire 3 spell for no WP).<br /> <br /> 9. Psychic Powers can now be used in rituals to combine them with hedge magic/quao/other psi-powers/etc, but require Synergy(the Psychic Power) Dot score greater than or equal to the highest dot power used(Synergy 4 is required to make a ritual using Divination 2 + Clairvoyance 4 and/or Divination 4 + Clairvoyance 2). The Ritual Psychic Merit allows you to bypass this.<br /> <br /> 10. Sorcerers are their own crossover splat, Not mage lackeys(more WOD Sorcerer independents in the same vein as Amenti or Wan Kuei{with different secret societies, didn't really like the ones in WOD Sorcerer}, Less Sorcerer revised mage style ghouls/kinfolk)<br /> <br /> (Rules continued moved from lower post):<br /> <br /> 11. Rather than have &quot;power&quot; be a separate aspect you have to buy into with successes, make it what sets the difficulty.<br /> <br /> Example: in normal Sorcerer Revised rules, you have to declare before the role how many successes you're allowed to buy into each aspect and that determines difficulty. A sorcerer with hellfire 5 that wants to spend 5 successes on damage, Type of damage, area, or distance has to roll against difficulty 9, while the same sorcerer just wants to be able to spend successes up to 3 rolls against difficulty 7. This rule makes it so that using higher path powers is exponentially more difficult than using lower path powers, and using lower path powers result in useless successes. Both of which are frustrating to players.<br /> <br /> In my system the above sorcerer would simply choose how much damage he want s to do, and roll against that difficulty to determine successes they want to spent. In this system, a sorcerer will have to sacrifice Fancy Damage/Area/Range for power(and vice versa) or spend mana. This way they aren't arbitrarily crippled.<br /> <br /> 12. Change dice-pool of sorcery to Attribute + Path Rating. Mostly to simplify the system and further reflect the ease by which humans learn human magic.(As you can probably tell, I stole the Idea from wraith. whose arcanoi are weaker than normal supernatural's abilities, but are bought at 3X Current dot rating)<br /> <br /> 13. Change the dicepool for psychic powers from Attribute + Ability to Permanent Willpower.<br /> <br /> 14. Change the sorcerer &quot;base&quot; difficulty of paths to 3 + Path rating(same as vampire thaumaturgy).<br /> <br /> 15. Have sorcerers use the same base stat spread as all supernaturals(Attributes 7/5/3, abilities 13/9/5, backgrounds totaling 7 dots, and 15 freebies). Not sure if they should use the sorcerer standards 5 numina dots, Mage/optional rule sorcerer 6 numina dots, or follow vampire's 3 starting dots with other rules considered","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 09-08-2018, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T15:04:32-07:00","id":1240601,"title":"","content":"What are you intending to Balance them with? Are you running a Generic mishmash of &quot;play whatever you want' or is it &quot;Sorcerers and... X&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T15:47:06-07:00","id":1240616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1240601#post1240601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you intending to Balance them with? Are you running a Generic mishmash of &quot;play whatever you want' or is it &quot;Sorcerers and... X&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Generic I guess? I'm trying to set up a &quot;One world of darkness&quot; setting, but I'm just starting off by throwing out any attempt to marry the cosmologies. Basically, No splat has the whole picture, Every faction of every splat has their own idea of &quot;what Really happened&quot;, and tagging along with any splat you'll be able experience their side of things(which will be rather confusing for beings like mages that Think They've managed to map the penumbra only to follow a werewolf for 5 minutes and discover half a dozen places he's never seen before that they apparently frequent often.)<br /> <br /> Basically, The world of darkness is a world with an infinite number of overlapping and parallel timelines, an infinite expanse of space where various points exist in multiple(or even the same) locations at once, Multiple parallel spiritual dimensions that embody archetypes of everything that did/does/could have exist(ed) simultaneously, a theoretically infinite number of lifeforms all generating their own internal parallel dimension via simple mental existence, and several forces of nature that temporarily/permanently change the properties of every force of nature(including themselves) at unpredictable intervals/in unpredictable ways simply by force of existing/not existing(possibly all simultaneously at once).<br /> <br /> Anyone who thinks they have the &quot;Big Picture&quot; in that mess is just wrong, even if they're right. Especially if they're right.<br /> <br /> My focus as a ST is just to create inter-splat politics, relevant to the game, to embody the fact that all those supernaturals exist and are aware of each other. I'm just re-balancing Sorcerer because Hedge magic has varied wildly in viability depending on edition and what gameline it's attached to(of which I very miffed to see that the recent trend seems to be writers nerfing an already starved power set.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T16:09:20-07:00","id":1240626,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to look at it on a purely mechanical level. From my perspective I think each of the big splats is its own &quot;tier&quot; of power level so when running mixed games at the very least I try to decide what tier we are at and adjust other splats accordingly. If we are running Mage Tier, for example Kindred are starting with more than three disciplines.<br /> <br /> So I'm having trouble deciding where to balance things.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I guess I'll ask a couple of generic points:<br /> <br /> I'd personally reduce Qiao cost to bring them in line with the rest.<br /> <br /> How are you handling Hybrids: Sorcerers who are something else(like Revenants, Kinfolk, Kinain) do they buy things like their related splat... or the &quot;Lol you're sidekick 20 xp per level ghoul!<br /> <br /> Coming from the other direction, supernatural who are also sorcerers, do you allow this? Do they get the same perks. Does that mean a Kitsune could learn Qiaos?<br /> <br /> Or do you just throw the whole thing out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T16:55:57-07:00","id":1240638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1240626#post1240626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to look at it on a purely mechanical level. From my perspective I think each of the big splats is its own &quot;tier&quot; of power level so when running mixed games at the very least I try to decide what tier we are at and adjust other splats accordingly. If we are running Mage Tier, for example Kindred are starting with more than three disciplines.<br /> <br /> So I'm having trouble deciding where to balance things.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I guess I'll ask a couple of generic points:<br /> <br /> I'd personally reduce Qiao cost to bring them in line with the rest.<br /> <br /> How are you handling Hybrids: Sorcerers who are something else(like Revenants, Kinfolk, Kinain) do they buy things like their related splat... or the &quot;Lol you're sidekick 20 xp per level ghoul!<br /> <br /> Coming from the other direction, supernatural who are also sorcerers, do you allow this? Do they get the same perks. Does that mean a Kitsune could learn Qiaos?<br /> <br /> Or do you just throw the whole thing out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was kinda hoping that my players don't try to play hybrids, but since it's still a possibility I guess I'd run it with some house rules.<br /> <br /> 1. Only one &quot;Heritage&quot; per character(likely as a merit)<br /> <br /> 2. Mana acting as that characters &quot;Magic pool&quot; for some powers(Glamour for kinnians, Gnosis for kinfolk), Unless inappropriate(revenants, and dhampires/dhampyrs would use their own life force like shih, with no mana substitution. It's Suppose to be a curse after all.)<br /> <br /> 3. Some Hedge magics can &quot;Raise the bar&quot; for some powers, Alchemy 5 for example can give you the first 3 dots of a discipline(which I think would be a good enough excuse to allow buying disciplines up to 3 a vampire out of clan values). It can do dito for gifts,(and probably mummy Hekau?) but not &quot;purely Spiritual&quot; abilities(like demon lores, wraith arcanois, some wan kuei abilities{soul and chi arts specifically}, or changeling powers). Mage Spheres become an odd duck as you can already learn any appropriate rote if you have the corresponding paths to substitute.<br /> <br /> 4. Use The Nephilim/Laham Merit in Book of secrets/path of screams books as a viable way to run DTF nephilim(gen 7 mana a day, gets 7 &quot;points&quot; to spend on up to 4 apocolypic form abilities they have always on{not able to retract claws or re-absorb scales}, not access to demon lores{which In-setting, having faith 7 that you can tap from birth is already very powerful in DTF's thrall system.} It also doesn't keep you from awakening or using paths{It's in fact an excuse to start as a mage or sorcerer})<br /> <br /> Beyond having the &quot;Mana(Glamour)&quot; specialized background, I'm not sure why a kinnian would learn hedge magic. As far as Hybrids go, a kinnian with a half-decent supply of glamour is in league with many other mid -tier full splats(even many changelings, most characters aren't going to max out 6 arts and a glamour 5 cap is still a very decent dice pool)<br /> <br /> Also any character with the &quot;Channeling&quot; power is already a &quot;medium&quot; possibly already more powerful than the WTO version. Other than spectre bestowments(Which isn't so much hedge magic as malfean infernalism. Which is a Whole different beast all together).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 07-30-2018, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T18:48:46-07:00","id":1240673,"title":"","content":"Would you have a ghoul sorcerer buy disciplines at Ghoul cost or Kindred cost?(same really with dhampyr/revenant etc)<br /> <br /> There are big splat supernaturals that can buy sorcery would you lower costs for them as well and do they have the option to learn Qiaos?<br /> <br /> As for why a Kinain might pick up sorcery because there's stuff Arts and realms just can't do that sorcery can, pretty much that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T20:03:59-07:00","id":1240700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1240673#post1240673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you have a ghoul sorcerer buy disciplines at Ghoul cost or Kindred cost?(same really with dhampyr/revenant etc)<br /> <br /> There are big splat supernaturals that can buy sorcery would you lower costs for them as well and do they have the option to learn Qiaos?<br /> <br /> As for why a Kinain might pick up sorcery because there's stuff Arts and realms just can't do that sorcery can, pretty much that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have the ghoul/alchemist choose a clan and buy their disciplines up to 3 dots at kindred out of clan. Blood magic as an exception, being kindred out of clan up to 5 dots. Mostly as it's ruled in various books that thuam, necromancy, and koldun are different from normal disciplines. IE: beast can't use blood magic in frenzy as of v20 core and DAV tome of secrets allows mortals to learn blood magic using health levels or blood sacrifices for vitae costs. So, if by VTM, mortals can use them anyway; why not?<br /> <br /> Notably the same exception exists in Dhampyrs/wan kuei(who I'd apply the same discipline rules, minus chi/soul arts noted as banned for dhampyrs) with the Chi Arts feng shui and (the astronomy/divination/luck manipulation one who's name escapes me), mortals(and dhampyrs) can learn both.<br /> <br /> Technically it's entirely rules legal to build a mortal character with thaum paths and chi arts by normal rules(good luck explaining that one to your ST).<br /> <br /> Also give supernaturals the normal sorcerery xp cost(if they can buy it at all, like kitsune/bastet with the cat/fox magic merit), this magic shouldn't come naturally to them(or at all in the case of vampires and wan kuei). They also have their own powers that are cheaper even if not able to create the exact effects of hedge magic/pychics/quao.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 08-26-2018, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T01:33:51-07:00","id":1248933,"title":"","content":"(Additional rules moved to main post)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 09-08-2018, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T07:50:30-07:00","id":1248957,"title":"","content":"If you want to do sorcerer's proper, my recommendation is to just simulate the Paths using Minor Spheres described in Mage Storyteller Handbook.<br /> Doesn't fix the whole issue where spells do less damage as you go up in power, but Mage also does that.<br /> Without completely rehauling the system, I'd say the minor spheres are the best you'll get.<br /> <br /> One of these days I'm going to finish writing that Sorcerer's Handbook 20th Edition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T11:06:26-07:00","id":1248982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1248933#post1248933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For another I forgot to add:<br /> <br /> <br /> 13. Change the dicepool for psychic powers from Attribute + Ability to Permanent Willpower.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This might work to some degree if people have only a single psychic abilitiy, but becomes massively unbalanced in S:Rev where characters are encouraged to build a number of them.<br /> <br /> However, one might steal what has occasionally been used. Roll becomes Attribute + (Power). This would make it easier to define when different styles are in play. I doubt Circe, Dr. M, and Kang the Brain all used the same skillset to use Shapeshifting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T18:05:19-07:00","id":1249042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1248957#post1248957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to do sorcerer's proper, my recommendation is to just simulate the Paths using Minor Spheres described in Mage Storyteller Handbook.<br /> Doesn't fix the whole issue where spells do less damage as you go up in power, but Mage also does that.<br /> Without completely rehauling the system, I'd say the minor spheres are the best you'll get.<br /> <br /> One of these days I'm going to finish writing that Sorcerer's Handbook 20th Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this goes against the idea of making sorcerers a separate thing entirely than mages. I think giving them &quot;lesser spheres&quot; puts them squarely into &quot;mages, but worse/crippled&quot; the way ghouls/kinfolk are to their respective splats. The entire reason for &quot;buffing&quot; sorcerers is to make them competitive with more powerful splats by making them cheaper/easier to use and not haphazardly tacking them onto another splat like Sorcerer Revised did to WOD Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1248982#post1248982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might work to some degree if people have only a single psychic abilitiy, but becomes massively unbalanced in S:Rev where characters are encouraged to build a number of them.<br /> <br /> However, one might steal what has occasionally been used. Roll becomes Attribute + (Power). This would make it easier to define when different styles are in play. I doubt Circe, Dr. M, and Kang the Brain all used the same skillset to use Shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The willpower thing is more to make psychics mechanically different from sorcerers and shih.(pychics using willpower, hedge magic using attribute + Power, and quao using attribute + Ability). I also don't really see it as overpowered, psychic powers are weaker than disciplines, gifts, etc. of the same level even with a larger/cheaper dicepool and are far less flexible than hedge magic. So my reasoning behind the separation is psychic powers having an single dicepool do to lower power and less flexability than other numina, hedge magic having wraith-like dicepools to compensate lowerpower but greater flexability, and quao having more standard dicepools do to being the most powerful of the numina and to reflect the years of training even the basic abilities require.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T13:53:44-07:00","id":1249775,"title":"","content":"How would you run True Faith?<br /> <br /> Can Mages have Sorcery in your rules? Personally I've always been for it, IMO it makes sense for a Mage to learn some static magic as a sort of... side interest. It's a distraction really since that EXP could go towards Arete or spheres, but knowing a path is a great way to work when you are knee deep in Paradox. If no, then how are you compensating them if they Awaken?<br /> <br /> Can Vampires learn &quot;normal&quot; Sorcery? If you're using the Sorcerer published rules then no... what about the &quot;embrace&quot; rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T16:14:49-07:00","id":1249826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1249042#post1249042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this goes against the idea of making sorcerers a separate thing entirely than mages. I think giving them &quot;lesser spheres&quot; puts them squarely into &quot;mages, but worse/crippled&quot; the way ghouls/kinfolk are to their respective splats. The entire reason for &quot;buffing&quot; sorcerers is to make them competitive with more powerful splats by making them cheaper/easier to use and not haphazardly tacking them onto another splat like Sorcerer Revised did to WOD Sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Removal of Paradox but giving them &quot;lesser spheres&quot; goes a long way to making them compete with Mages. Hell, the ability to be overt is an extremely useful ability. Sure they're more narrow ranged, but the Sphere of Elemental Power is a lot more impressive when you can throw fireballs all day long.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T16:30:42-07:00","id":1249831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1249775#post1249775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you run True Faith?<br /> <br /> Can Mages have Sorcery in your rules? Personally I've always been for it, IMO it makes sense for a Mage to learn some static magic as a sort of... side interest. It's a distraction really since that EXP could go towards Arete or spheres, but knowing a path is a great way to work when you are knee deep in Paradox. If no, then how are you compensating them if they Awaken?<br /> <br /> Can Vampires learn &quot;normal&quot; Sorcery? If you're using the Sorcerer published rules then no... what about the &quot;embrace&quot; rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd do what sorcerer revised suggests and let the turn their path/psionics/quao back into XP they can use to buy disciplines/sphere dots(probably with a limit per session of how many dots they can buy, to reflectthat they still need to re-learn how to do things with a new magic system).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1249826#post1249826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Removal of Paradox but giving them &quot;lesser spheres&quot; goes a long way to making them compete with Mages. Hell, the ability to be overt is an extremely useful ability. Sure they're more narrow ranged, but the Sphere of Elemental Power is a lot more impressive when you can throw fireballs all day long.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still tying them up with mage mechanically. If my ST gave me a list of lesser spheres to pick from and said that I won't get paradox for using them, I'd ask why we weren't just playing mage. It also ties it to mages more broken rules like wonder creation, which sorcerer doesn't have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T16:52:13-07:00","id":1249838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1249831#post1249831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd do what sorcerer revised suggests and let the turn their path/psionics/quao back into XP they can use to buy disciplines/sphere dots(probably with a limit per session of how many dots they can buy, to reflectthat they still need to re-learn how to do things with a new magic system).</div> </div> </div> </div>It taking time is a great idea. And it makes sense to convert between things which are reasonable. Time becomes Celerity, Hellfire becomes Lure of Flames, Alchemy becomes Path of Blood, Correspondence/Teleportation becomes Path of Mercury...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T16:59:39-07:00","id":1249839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1249838#post1249838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It taking time is a great idea. And it makes sense to convert between things which are reasonable. Time becomes Celerity, Hellfire becomes Lure of Flames, Alchemy becomes Path of Blood, Correspondence/Teleportation becomes Path of Mercury...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also a big reason why more mystical vamps(at least those aware sorcerers exist) hunt down sorcerers/mages for embrace. A powerful, quick learning student of the arcane is an apprentice most tremere and some koldunes would/have already killed for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T22:55:48-07:00","id":1249889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1249838#post1249838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It taking time is a great idea. And it makes sense to convert between things which are reasonable. Time becomes Celerity, Hellfire becomes Lure of Flames, Alchemy becomes Path of Blood, Correspondence/Teleportation becomes Path of Mercury...</div> </div> </div> </div>Time should become Temporis.<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't Alchemy become Alchemy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T02:49:33-07:00","id":1249912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1249889#post1249889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time should become Temporis.<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't Alchemy become Alchemy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it would depend on the ST's call. Time could become Temporis of course, but the ST might not want a unique Discipline being reinvented this way; if embracing any Mage with Time will make Temporis, then it's hard to justify only the True Brujah having it. And Celerity is a form of time magic, that's why it doesn't give momentum or effect friction etc.<br /> <br /> A good solution might be to say that as a rule, the Disciplines acquired by Sorcerers and Mages as they relearn post embrace can't be naturally taught to other Vampires in most cases. They're not true Inceptors like the 3rd Generation and thinbloods. Their version of Temporis/Protean/Obtenebration is a weird quirk that can be taught to Mage-cum-Vampires who had similar practices as a Mage.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer Revised mentions that Alchemy transitions well into Path of Blood since they're both related to foundational properties. Path of Blood is the simplest form of blood magic and is easily understood by a master of alchemy; they could easily discover it while experimenting with their own blood in their old alchemical gear.<br /> <br /> Besides, path of alchemy in blood magic just... converts things from one thing to another, and does it so slowly that it might as well be a ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T03:45:27-07:00","id":1249921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1249912#post1249912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerer Revised mentions that Alchemy transitions well into Path of Blood since they're both related to foundational properties. Path of Blood is the simplest form of blood magic and is easily understood by a master of alchemy; they could easily discover it while experimenting with their own blood in their old alchemical gear.<br /> <br /> Besides, path of alchemy in blood magic just... converts things from one thing to another, and does it so slowly that it might as well be a ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't mana manipulation be a better fit for transitioning into Path of blood? I also think there'll be quite a bit of overlap between how different paths of sorcery translate into thaumaturgy(is helfire XP better spent on lure of flames or path of levinbolt?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T20:09:03-07:00","id":1250384,"title":"","content":"How many people actually have either Sorcerer books? Not that many. Most people have a core book or two and an equally small number of supplements.<br /> <br /> The easiest way to make some mortal linear sorcerers is to just adapt the V20 system.<br /> <br /> It's not that hard. Change the blood pool to <s>mana</s> quintessence pool. Characters start out with a pool of ten as level one apprentices and can expand their pools with seekings of escalating difficulty, eventually becoming level 13 Grandmasters with pools of 50. Give them access to Thaumaturgy, Necromancy and whatever disciplines are appropriate for your chronicle. Chimestry, Obeah, Temporis, Auspex, Obfuscate, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 09-01-2018, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T06:15:28-07:00","id":1250437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1250384#post1250384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many people actually have either Sorcerer books? Not that many. Most people have a core book or two and an equally small number of supplements.<br /> <br /> The easiest way to make some mortal linear sorcerers is to just adapt the V20 system.<br /> <br /> It's not that hard. Change the blood pool to <s>mana</s> quintessence pool. Characters start out with a pool of ten as level one apprentices and can expand their pools with seekings of escalating difficulty, eventually becoming level 13 grandmasters with pools of 50. Give them access to thaumaturgy, necromancy and whatever disciplines are appropriate for your chronicle. Chimestry, Obeah, Temporis, Auspex, Obfuscate, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems overpowered honestly. It also seems more like a substitute for Mage than sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers also don't have anything to do with seekings in either of their books, that's a mage thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T06:38:58-07:00","id":1250440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1250437#post1250437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems overpowered honestly. It also seems more like a substitute for Mage than sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers also don't have anything to do with seekings in either of their books, that's a mage thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe and maybe, but real mages are still stronger, and at least it does work and is easy to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T08:21:34-07:00","id":1250454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1250440#post1250440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe and maybe, but real mages are still stronger, and at least it does work and is easy to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easier maybe, but they'd be steam-rolling a lot of other splats. <br /> <br /> I kinda like sorcerer because it fills a similar role as mages, but without the massively prominent ways to break the game in crossover. You won't see a sorcerer traveling the umbra in huge ether-ships that do 70 levels of aggrevated damage to everything in a 3 mile radius just by it's energy shields alone.<br /> <br /> It also comes down to philosophy a bit. Mage's philosophy is that &quot;Yes, you can do X&quot; with most of the conflict stemming from the consequences of your actions and the inevitable punch that happens when you play god. It's setting also is entirely based on sophism, &quot;everyone is right&quot;, &quot;perception is everything&quot;, and &quot;the modern world is limiting people's potential&quot; are very prominent(and in my opinion, Heavy-Handed) themes. Magic is easy, it's flexible on the fly and can be made more powerful with time/resources. The only problem is that learning magic is hard, but all it requires is some intense navel gazing.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer has the opposite philosophy. Magic is Hard in sorcerer. Paths are flexible, but not all powerful and blending them required time, training and rituals. A hellfire user can throw fireballs with a snap of his fingers, he could probably change it's shape so that it looks like a firey bird flying toward his target, but he can't use it to stop bullets mid-air. Magic is only flexible when you give it time, but it's never going to make you a demi-god. Learning magic however is simple, it's a set of laws inherit to the world that you must study to learn. You must however set aside your worldview to learn how the world Actually works.<br /> <br /> If I'm to be honest, I'm biased. I don't like mage's view of the world. I love it's endless possiblities and rich lore, but It doesn't marry with other splats well unless you blatently ignore it's core premise. I also can't stomach it's view on the modern world, how it trumpets &quot;freedom&quot; by literally making reality based on who perceives it and trying to sell off things like &quot;technology&quot;, &quot;modernization&quot;, and &quot;the scientific method&quot; as poisonous to free thought or just magic in disguise.<br /> <br /> As a person who works with science/technology for a living and have actively studied the subject for my own enjoyment, this sort of thing makes me understand how an african american man seeing &quot;black face&quot; in early american plays and movies must have felt(Yes, I get it's just a game, but it is a game that preys on peoples ignorance of technology to equate it with magic. It's like watching Clarke's third law i action). I guess that makes me a technocrat that &quot;Drank the Kool-Aid&quot; so what the heck do I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T19:13:41-07:00","id":1250605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1249831#post1249831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're still tying them up with mage mechanically. If my ST gave me a list of lesser spheres to pick from and said that I won't get paradox for using them, I'd ask why we weren't just playing mage. It also ties it to mages more broken rules like wonder creation, which sorcerer doesn't have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they do? Where do you think the Technocrats get most of their equipment from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T03:21:17-07:00","id":1250694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1250605#post1250605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they do? Where do you think the Technocrats get most of their equipment from?</div> </div> </div> </div>I must contest that, while a bit vague, the path of enchanting doesn't give you the ability to make things nearly as powerful as wonders.<br /> <br /> Even at 5 dots, going from the examples, it can create an item that can add 5 dice too any role, add 4 successes or subtract the same from an enemy role, or a single &quot;Story-Power&quot;(I.E. things that give you access to knowledges you wouldn't have like asking the ghost of an archmage a question. This is technically a plot device power, but in use it should probably just give 5 dice in the apropriate pool and allow the character to roll like they had said knowledge or other ability). In return for that, they have to pay heavy costs or give the item limitations that destroy the enchantment if not met(like taking 5 years of your life very time it's used, or being only able to use it 4 times a day or the enchantment is destroyed).<br /> <br /> A wonder on the other hand can be far more powerful, the only limitation on the dicepool it has is the amount of successes they get on a ritual(which with backgrounds like cult and sanctum, can easily exceed 20+ on a Starting Character), they only limit of a wonders effects is the spheres the mage has(Which isn't really a limitation in the technocracy, having large cabals of mages woking together to make the best equipment possible is the norm rather than the exception. Wonder creation is also a rote, one that can be put On a wonder, and thus automated), and It doesn't require any kind of drawback beyond paradox(which can be absorbed by a wonder, tracked, and transported away so that it never becomes a problem. The technocracy is especially capable of this, as they can have entire factories automated with a prime 5 rote and ready to &quot;clean&quot; any equipment on Mass).<br /> <br /> The technocracy already Has all the resources it needs to supply not only it's mages, but even it's citizens(extraordinary or otherwise) with a multitute of powerful wonders. That is in fact it's MO as well, as it integrates it's paradigm into the concensus By producing wonders, marketing them to the public, and then producing them On Mass. This is kind of why they already won.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T22:17:04-07:00","id":1250972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1250454#post1250454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Easier maybe, but they'd be steam-rolling a lot of other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how much XP you're giving them.<br /> <br /> The biggest advantage they'd have over a vampire with the same XP would be that they can walk around during the day, which is the same no matter what powers you give them.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, would be at a disadvantage at range, but they'd still be heavily favored if they managed to get close.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T10:12:56-07:00","id":1251085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1250972#post1250972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on how much XP you're giving them.<br /> <br /> The biggest advantage they'd have over a vampire with the same XP would be that they can walk around during the day, which is the same no matter what powers you give them.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, would be at a disadvantage at range, but they'd still be heavily favored if they managed to get close.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, if you make everything cost the same as vampire disciplines normally do, you end up playing a worse version of vampires. If you off-set the XP costs to make them able to compete, you end up making these, er, &quot;Blood Mages&quot; overpowered after longer periods of play.<br /> <br /> To start off with, you've got people who are stuck at 10 BP spent at 1 per turn with no easy way to replenish, who can't soak lethal or aggrevated damage, and have few discipline powers. If any of the previous statements are incorrect then you are just playing a vampire that can walk in sunlight. Playing a demi-vampire that's worse than a normal splat doesn't sound fun to me, and neither does playing a character that has all of the powers of a vampire with none of the draw-backs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 09-03-2018, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T21:27:25-07:00","id":1251272,"title":"","content":"Let me pipe in with support for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6383\" data-vbnamecard=\"6383\">Prometheas</a>' vision. Sorcery Paths are <i>not</i> \u201cMinor Spheres\u201d, and sorcerers are not \u201clesser mages\u201d. The fact that Paradox isn't a thing for sorcerers is part of that (and as part of the changes, I'd suggest striking SRev's statement about Sorcery flat-out failing when there are Sleeper witnesses around); but so is the progression: Sorcery Paths often make effects available earlier than the Spheres most similar to them would. And that's just on the crunch side of things; in terms of \u201cfluff\u201d, the whole point of Sorcery is that it's <i>not</i> about focused will altering reality; it's about learning and exploiting occult mysteries. And psychics are something else entirely, distinct from both. <br /> <br /> I'd go so far as to putting some serious consideration into whether hybrid Sorcerer/Mages are possible. If they aren't, it's because of a fundamental incompatibility between being a Mage and being a Sorcerer, <i>not</i> because Sorcery is a subset of the Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T16:55:33-07:00","id":1252393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1251272#post1251272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me pipe in with support for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6383\" data-vbnamecard=\"6383\">Prometheas</a>' vision. Sorcery Paths are <i>not</i> \u201cMinor Spheres\u201d, and sorcerers are not \u201clesser mages\u201d. The fact that Paradox isn't a thing for sorcerers is part of that (and as part of the changes, I'd suggest striking SRev's statement about Sorcery flat-out failing when there are Sleeper witnesses around); but so is the progression: Sorcery Paths often make effects available earlier than the Spheres most similar to them would. And that's just on the crunch side of things; in terms of \u201cfluff\u201d, the whole point of Sorcery is that it's <i>not</i> about focused will altering reality; it's about learning and exploiting occult mysteries. And psychics are something else entirely, distinct from both.<br /> <br /> I'd go so far as to putting some serious consideration into whether hybrid Sorcerer/Mages are possible. If they aren't, it's because of a fundamental incompatibility between being a Mage and being a Sorcerer, <i>not</i> because Sorcery is a subset of the Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>You must really learn to separate the difference between mechanics and fluff. It's easier to use mechanics of existing stuff than recreate the wheel. If you want to do it fast and loose, that's the easiest way to go about it, rather than fixing all of Sorcerer.<br /> That said, I'm not caring anymore as it's clear Prometheas hasn't read even the Sorcerer as he doesn't believe Sorcery can make Wonders, despite it quite literally being called out in the Sorcerer book so there's no point in continuing the argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":2414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","user":"theoutlander523","date":". 09-07-2018, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T19:06:30-07:00","id":1252421,"title":"","content":"Have <i>you</i> read <b>Sorcerer</b>? By that, I mean <b> World of Darkness: Sorcerer, the Hedge Magician's Handbook</b>, not <b>Sorcerer, Revised</b>. The latter had superior crunch, but its fluff left a lot to be desired and was inferior to the former's fluff. And it is primarily on <i>that</i> basis that I say that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6383\" data-vbnamecard=\"6383\">Prometheas</a> is essentially correct: the whole point of the fluff in Hedge Magician's Handbook was that sorcerers are <i>not</i> mage wannabees; they are their own thing, as separate from <b>Mage</b>'s \u201cEnlightened Will Shapes Reality\u201d metaphysics as vampires are. <br /> <br /> I'm happy to talk about SR where crunch is concerned; but when you're talking about the underlying philosophy of what a Sorcerer <i>is</i>, WoD:S is far superior.<br /> <br /> And no, sorcerers cannot create what mages call Wonders. They can create magical items; but the \u201cwonders\u201d they create are no more the same thing that mages create than are the magical items that other night folk make. (I just did a text search for \u201cWonder\u201d in SR to make sure I didn't overlook something; and while there are a couple of mentions of sorcerers sometimes being in <i>possession</i> of Wonders, there's no mention anywhere of them being able to <i>make</i> Wonders. The closest you get is a text box about \u201cTalismans vs. Talismans\u201d which says that, to a layperson, it's difficult at best to tell the difference between the two \u2014 which is <i>not</i> the same as saying that there <i>is</i> no difference.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-07-2018, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T01:43:29-07:00","id":1252459,"title":"","content":"Agreed with Dataweaver. Sorcerers believe in truth without paradox; they're discovering esoteric mysteries and taking the slow path. They're not Mage's natural servants or students. They're not wannabe Mages. Some do fit those molds of course, but some Mages are wannabe Garou/Cainites.<br /> <br /> Their magic being static is a great advantage and a great weakness. They're reliant on their own wits to survive. For them, the ability to bind a spirit and command it doesn't bring an innate ability to kill spirits. But to do what they do to spirits you'd need lots of Correspondence and Spirit, far more than most mages ever will.<br /> <br /> With that said, I'd make advancing your Paths cheaper and I'd make learning rituals simply take time, and require certain paths. Rituals should be the less static aspect of sorcery; coming up with new ones is just part of what people imagine when you think of a sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T11:27:05-07:00","id":1252558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers?p=1252393#post1252393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'm not caring anymore as it's clear Prometheas hasn't read even the Sorcerer as he doesn't believe Sorcery can make Wonders, despite it quite literally being called out in the Sorcerer book so there's no point in continuing the argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Dataweaver has pointed out, no sorcerer don't have the ability to make wonders by default. Unless you rule that any magical item made by any supernatural counts as a wonder(which, honestly, a given mage might think despite the fact they're mechanically different with dice on the table).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 01-04-2022, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}